# SSH remote workspace

`dsh-remote` is **desktop-owned built-in**: vendored fork `vendor/dsh-remote` (host half snapshot, `update.js` dropped, deps git-tracked under its `node_modules`), ensure `src/main/dsh-remote-desktop.js` writes `desktop-plugins/dsh-remote/desktop-dsh-remote.patch.yml` and junctions `profiles/web/node_modules/dsh-remote` → vendor source. Mounts via `--patch` on EVERY start (full + skip) only while `remoteWorkspaceEnabled` (default **on**, 界面设置「远程工作区」开关, flip restarts Harness) is true — off strips legacy managed blocks and deletes the overlay without vendor checks. Never write managed blocks to the user-owned `cordis.patch.yml`. Package name `dsh-remote` joins `DROPPED_BASENAMES` (catalog hidden, in-chat install rejected, `stripDroppedPlugins` every start); existing `$DSH_HOME/remote-workspaces` data (machines/known_hosts/mirrors/audit) is taken over by the built-in. Forensics flags absent-in-profile suspects `inBox`/`desktopRuntimeDamage`; disable list does not apply; ensure failure blocks start and skip cannot fix it.

Picker remote entry: `ui-directory-picker-browse` fork declares a new `single` remote-flow child hole and renders the 本机/远程 tab strip — remote client occupies it, empty hole = local-only (seam's native default). The upstream plugin's `priority: -100` hole-grab is NOT ported; 本机 tab behavior unchanged. All new UI is rewritten on `ui-primitives` / `--dsw-alias-*` tokens / typed dictionaries — the original ~160KB client is reference only.

Remote context is session-scoped: system prompt injects only while session cwd is inside a mirror; 20 `rw_*` tools satisfy `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{1,64}`; writes/removes/moves/forwards land in `audit.log`; `rw_sync`/`rw_push` three-way conflicts never silently overwrite; TOFU `accept-new` rejects changed host keys. Credentials + known_hosts + mirrors stay under `$DSH_HOME/remote-workspaces` — never `~/.dsh`; plaintext passwords are upstream behavior, DPAPI encryption is deferred. New settings section「远程工作区」— do NOT merge into phone `remote` (`ui-settings-remote`/`dshd-remote`) or confuse with `dsh-api-remotes` / upstream `packages/ssh/*`.

